              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Paula W"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Very simple, very tasty. Thank you. \nBTW when you change a recipe by decreasing the spices in it, well it's not quite fair to call it bland, now is it?"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Heather P"
            },
            "reviewBody": "First time making quinoa and I followed this recipe exactly as directed. I used Inca Red Quinoa, which came out perfect and delicious! My hub and I both had second servings, even. I did add a couple dashes of turmeric b/c it's good for the heart, but no modifications other than that. Great recipe!",
            "datePublished": "2018-08-23T18:47:22.607Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "kakw123"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Very tasty! My husband loved it too. I added some roasted carrots and onions in the final few minutes of cooking. I served this with pork tenderloin and it complemented the pork wonderfully. So easy and delicious. Thanks for this great recipe.",
            "datePublished": "2014-08-14T05:54:21.823Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Christine TB"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Fantastic! Even the two little kids love it! Instead of water, I added some bone broth that we have going in our slow cooker 24/7 during the winter months. As a result, ours was not as salty as I think it would have been had I used bullion, but this was easily rectified by adding a couple pinches of salt after cooking. I also used freshly grated ginger so there's a little extra spicy kick.",
            "datePublished": "2014-01-12T17:23:02.813Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Jajam"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I used the full amount of spice with white quinoa. What a great dish! Oops, I used my garam masala instead of Chinese 5-spice. Sorry...I just have to rate it because it was so fragrantly good. Both of these mixtures have many variations, so that will affect your outcome. I have seen 5-spice with cinnamon as the first ingredient, and others with szechuan pepper as the first! I like the garam masala on this site, and it is probably milder than most 5-spice recipes. I plan to make this on a regular basis.",
            "datePublished": "2013-04-04T15:03:14.497Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "3"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Barbara"
            },
            "reviewBody": "The Chinese five-spice flavor was over whelming. Unless you want a very strong flavor of 5-spice cut the amount added. I will make it again and add only enough 5-spice to taste a hint of it.",
            "datePublished": "2010-09-26T08:30:19.653Z"
          },
          {
